# Keep the Docker build context small and reproducible — the Dockerfiles rebuild from source.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
docs/
tools/
tests/
**/*.user

# All environment-specific appsettings are kept OUT of the image. The shared DB
# connection string is injected at runtime via .env (ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection),
# never baked in. Only the committed base appsettings.json is shipped.
**/appsettings.*.json

# Let the SDK bundled in the build image pick the .NET version. The repo's global.json
# pins a specific 9.0.3xx SDK band for local dev; excluding it here keeps the container
# build immune to the floating `sdk:9.0` tag drifting past that band.
global.json

# Runtime-only artifacts
.env
*.env
deploy.tar.gz
*.md

# Uploaded documents live in the `crms-storage` volume, never in the image.
src/CRMS.Web.Intranet/storage/
